{
  "id": "c-brl-cad-task-21-ubuntu",
  "snapshot": "BRL-CAD7.32.2",
  "instruction": "Use BRL-CAD to read the STEP input file(s) from the Desktop path(s): /home/user/Desktop/block_a.step, /home/user/Desktop/cyl_b.step. Read /home/user/Desktop/block_a.step and /home/user/Desktop/cyl_b.step. Reorient the cylinder so its axis is along Y and passes through the center of the block, then fuse it with the block. Finally cut a central through hole of diameter 10 mm along Z through the fused solid. Export exactly one STL mesh named /home/user/Desktop/out.stl to the output folder.",
  "source": "https://cadquery.readthedocs.io/en/latest/importexport.html https://cadquery.readthedocs.io/en/latest/genindex.html",
